My senior dev is begging me for a blank check for this 'Temporal' thing to orchestrate three background jobs that run once a day. I asked for an ROI and he sent me a 50-page whitepaper on 'durable execution'.
The sales rep says their "active-active geo-replication" is mission-critical, but we're a cat photo sharing app serving one city. I feel like I'm being sold a Ferrari to go grocery shopping.
So we're going to replace a free, open-source tool that works fine with a proprietary, expensive one that we don't have the skills to manage, just because a blog post said it was 'web scale'? Am I the only one who thinks this is insane?
The engineer keeps saying 'idempotency' and 'workflow replay' like it's magic. I asked him to explain it in business terms and he just stared at me blankly for a full minute. I am not signing this PO.
You sold me on 'free open-source PostHog', now you're telling me it needs a full-time engineer to babysit its database and our bill for the underlying cloud VMs is five grand a month?
