Our self-hosted PostHog instance is down again, and the one person who knew how to fix it just quit. I thought 'open source' was supposed to save us money, not hold our analytics hostage.
We bought Databricks to avoid vendor lock-in with Snowflake, but now all our data is in this proprietary 'Delta Lake' format and we're more locked in than ever.
The engineer says the software is free, but the architecture diagram he showed me requires a new Kubernetes cluster, a managed database, and an on-call rotation. This is the most expensive 'free' software I've ever seen.
