My Datadog bill just came in and it's higher than my payroll. Are we monitoring a business or funding a small country?
The sales guy sold me a 'single pane of glass', but my engineers have created 5,000 dashboards and now no one can find anything. It's a single pane of shattered, confusing glass.
My team says we need to hire a full-time DBA because our queries are slow, but isn't this the most popular open-source database in the world? Why isn't it just fast out of the box?
So we have to take the entire application offline for a whole weekend to perform a major version upgrade, and if anything goes wrong we might lose data? And this is what you call a 'mature' database?
My engineers say they can't debug production without shipping terabytes of logs, and now my Datadog bill for 'log ingestion and indexing' is literally my biggest single line-item expense after salaries.
